<!-- page: 1 -->

According the ODF 1\.2 specification\, consecutive whitespace characters \(space\, tab\, newline\) should be collapsed to one space within \<text\:p\> and \<text\:h\> elements\. The \<text\:s\> element is not considered for collapsing\. In this document\, several combinations of spaces\, text and \<text\:span\> elements are shown\. The number of spaces that should be displayed between the \'a\' and \'b\' characters is printed at the end of each line\.

# Simple spaces

no space

ab \<span\>a\<\/span\>\<span\>b\<\/span\> 0

one space

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\>\<span\>b\<\/span\> 1

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\> \<span\>b\<\/span\> 1

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\>\<span\> b\<\/span\> 1

two consecutive spaces

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\> \<span\> b\<\/span\> 1

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\>\<span\> b\<\/span\> 1

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\> \<span\>b\<\/span\> 1

three consecutive spaces 

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\> \<span\> b\<\/span\> 1

# Spaces and \<s\/\>

no space

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\>\<s\/\>\<span\>b\<\/span\> 1

one space

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\>\<s\/\>\<span\>b\<\/span\> 2

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\> \<s\/\>\<span\>b\<\/span\> 2

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\>\<s\/\> \<span\>b\<\/span\> 2

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\>\<s\/\>\<span\> b\<\/span\> 2

two spaces

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\> \<s\/\>\<span\>b\<\/span\> 2

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\>\<s\/\> \<span\>b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\>\<s\/\>\<span\> b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\> \<s\/\> \<span\>b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\> \<s\/\>\<span\> b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\>\<s\/\> \<span\> b\<\/span\> 2

three spaces

a b \<span\>a\<\/span\> \<s\/\> \<span\> b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\>\<s\/\> \<span\> b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\> \<s\/\>\<span\> b\<\/span\> 3

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\> \<s\/\> \<span\>b\<\/span\> 3

four spaces

a b \<span\>a \<\/span\> \<s\/\> \<span\> b\<\/span\> 3